2) LONGEST PALINDROMIC SUBSEQUENCE (LPS)

🔥 Very important

Asked in DP rounds

Variation of LCS

Loved by interviewers because it tests DP thinking

📌 Problem Statement

Given a string s, find the length of the Longest Palindromic Subsequence.

A palindromic sequence reads the same forward and backward.

Note:

Characters do not need to be contiguous

This is NOT substring

✍ Example
Input: "bbbab"
Output: 4


Explanation:
The longest palindromic subsequence is "bbbb"

🧠 Key Observation (INTERVIEW GOLD)

LPS of a string = LCS(string, reverse(string))

Because:

A palindrome reads same forward & backward

Matching characters in string and its reverse form palindromes

🧮 Algorithm

Let rev = reverse of string s

Compute LCS(s, rev) using Dynamic Programming

Result is the Longest Palindromic Subsequence length

📐 DP Definition
dp[i][j] = LCS length of first i chars of s
           and first j chars of reversed string

💻 Java Code
public class LongestPalindromicSubsequence {

    public static int longestPalindromeSubseq(String s) {

        String rev = new StringBuilder(s).reverse().toString();
        int n = s.length();

        int[][] dp = new int[n + 1][n + 1];

        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {

                if (s.charAt(i - 1) == rev.charAt(j - 1)) {
                    dp[i][j] = 1 + dp[i - 1][j - 1];
                } else {
                    dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i - 1][j], dp[i][j - 1]);
                }
            }
        }
        return dp[n][n];
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String s = "bbbab";
        System.out.println(longestPalindromeSubseq(s));
    }
}

